  "title": "An honest practice card",
  "sourceHash": "sha256:e454e4c2fbfbf8726a59add760cdc68421f53ab9a66485de8ed41be94c53737f",
  "outline": [
    {
      "heading": "How not to write it",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Practice catalogues often contain promises: the practice \"will heal\", \"opens abilities\", \"gives answers to any question\", \"clears all suppressed emotions\".",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "What the practice serves",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Sessions in the morning, an outing in the afternoon that has nothing to do with them.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Fields of an honest card",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Template: practice card.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Who brings what",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "It helps to split the \"what it needs\" list into three parts: what the venue provides (the hall, mats, sometimes blankets), what the leader brings (a gong, a speaker, oils, candles) and what the guest packs (a water bottle, warm clothes, their own mat if the venue does not provide them).",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Scent, smoke and sound",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Essential oils, incense, sage and palo santo, a loud gong do not suit everyone.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Care next to the mat",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Next to the group — water, tissues and a couple of spare blankets.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Example: an intense breathwork practice",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Format — group.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    },
    {
      "heading": "Example: a pair practice with touch",
      "points": [
        {
          "text": "Format — pair.",
          "origin": "extract"
        }
      ],
      "children": []
    }
  ],
